<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mudhoji II Bhonsle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1796–1840</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Appa Sahib</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mudhoji II Bhonsle, known as Appa Sahib, was ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagpur">Nagpur</a> from 1816 to 1818, first as regent for his cousin Parsoji, whom he is believed to have had murdered. Having signed a subsidiary alliance with the British, he attacked their residency at Sitabuldi in November 1817 and was defeated. He was deposed, escaped from custody and died in exile at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mudhoji-ii-bhonsle.jpg" alt="Mudhoji II Bhonsle" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mudhoji_Bhosale_II_Appasaheb.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
